      "anchor": {
        "kind": "smart",
        "lineCache": "export class AnchorRepairQueue implements vscode.Disposable {",
        "contextBefore": [],
        "contextAfter": [],
        "lastUpdatedLine": 57,
        "nonce": 0
      },
      "label": "AnchorRepairQueue — the main background work queue",
      "note": "PRIMARY work queue. Defers git-history-based smart-anchor repair OFF the file-open hot path so it doesn't burn CPU or block the UI. Lives in the EXTENSION (not core). Implements vscode.Disposable. Holds TWO internal queues: `pending` (full repairs, gated by the `agenticBookmarks.autoRepair` setting) and `pendingDeepFlex` (display-only deep-flex position checks, NOT gated by autoRepair). CPU-friendly mechanisms: 500ms debounce, 3000ms per-file timeout, sequential processing yielding to the event loop (setTimeout 0) between every file AND every anchor, and cancellation when files are closed or edited.",
      "createdAt": 1779287002259,
      "source": "mcp"
    },
    {
      "id": "C7QamjIw",
      "fileId": "cPqQBMDw",
      "groupId": "grM5t0mU",
      "target": {
        "uri": "packages/extension/src/repairQueue.ts"
      },
      "anchor": {
        "kind": "smart",
        "lineCache": "const DEBOUNCE_MS = 500;",
        "contextBefore": [],
        "contextAfter": [],
        "lastUpdatedLine": 54,
        "nonce": 0
      },
      "label": "Throttle constants: 500ms debounce + 3000ms per-file timeout",
      "note": "The two knobs that keep the queue from overwhelming the system: DEBOUNCE_MS=500 (batch rapid enqueue calls) and PER_FILE_TIMEOUT_MS=3000 (a single file's repair pass can't run longer than 3s; checked against a deadline in processFile).",
      "createdAt": 1779287005289,
      "source": "mcp"
    },
    {
      "id": "NnEDjpOr",
      "fileId": "cPqQBMDw",
      "groupId": "grM5t0mU",
      "target": {
        "uri": "packages/extension/src/repairQueue.ts"
      },
      "anchor": {
        "kind": "smart",
        "lineCache": "  enqueue(docUri: string): void {",
        "contextBefore": [],
        "contextAfter": [],
        "lastUpdatedLine": 72,
        "nonce": 0
      },
      "label": "enqueue() — add a file for full anchor repair (autoRepair-gated)",
      "note": "Work item = a file URI whose broken anchors need repair. Bails immediately if `agenticBookmarks.autoRepair` is off. Adds the URI to `pending`, clears any \"edited\" flag, and resets the 500ms debounce timer so a burst of opens collapses into one processing pass.",
      "createdAt": 1779287008059,
      "source": "mcp"
    },
    {
      "id": "C02dmByf",
      "fileId": "cPqQBMDw",
      "groupId": "grM5t0mU",
      "target": {
        "uri": "packages/extension/src/repairQueue.ts"
      },
      "anchor": {
        "kind": "smart",
        "lineCache": "  enqueueDeepFlexOnly(docUri: string): void {",
        "contextBefore": [],
        "contextAfter": [],
        "lastUpdatedLine": 97,
        "nonce": 0
      },
      "label": "enqueueDeepFlexOnly() — second queue, display-only, NOT autoRepair-gated",
      "note": "Work item = a file URI with anchors whose lineCache matched but whose context fell outside the resolution flex window (flex=5). Runs a wider repair window (FLEX_REPAIR_WINDOW=100). Always runs because it only updates in-memory display position; the actual disk write (applyRepair) is still gated by autoRepair inside the loop. Separate debounce timer + separate `pendingDeepFlex` set, allowed to run concurrently with the main queue.",
      "createdAt": 1779287011393,
      "source": "mcp"
    },
    {
      "id": "wiWuHgig",
      "fileId": "cPqQBMDw",
      "groupId": "grM5t0mU",
      "target": {
        "uri": "packages/extension/src/repairQueue.ts"
      },
      "anchor": {
        "kind": "smart",
        "lineCache": "  private async processQueue(): Promise<void> {",
        "contextBefore": [],
        "contextAfter": [],
        "lastUpdatedLine": 145,
        "nonce": 0
      },
      "label": "processQueue() — drains pending one file at a time, yielding between each",
      "note": "The drain loop. `processing` flag guards against re-entrancy. Pulls one URI at a time from `pending`, skips files edited since enqueue, re-checks the autoRepair setting, processes the file, then `await setTimeout(0)` to yield to the event loop before the next file — this is what spreads CPU cost over time.",
      "createdAt": 1779287014035,
      "source": "mcp"
    },
    {
      "id": "lReBPf7B",
