      },
      "anchor": {
        "kind": "smart",
        "lineCache": "    getRepairQueue()?.enqueue(docUri);",
        "contextBefore": [],
        "contextAfter": [],
        "lastUpdatedLine": 141,
        "nonce": 0
      },
      "label": "Producer: file-open path enqueues into the repair queue",
      "note": "The main producer side of the queue. When a document's anchors are resolved (on open), this enqueues the URI for full repair (enqueue) and for deep-flex checking (enqueueDeepFlexOnly). This is the \"hot path\" the queue exists to keep light — both calls just register the URI and return; the heavy git work is deferred behind the debounce.",
      "createdAt": 1779287022454,
      "source": "mcp"
    },
